    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2ceef1f7_ca3b60d9",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/Device.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 2491,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000014
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-26T05:37:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027d like if possible to avoid the idea that \"a device has a feature level\" after initialization, even though it\u0027s very useful during initialization. (In the JS API feature levels are only relevant during initialization - after requestAdapter and before requestDevice. Once you have a device, all that matters is the features and limits of the device.)\n\nPerhaps in `DeviceBase::DeviceBase` we could have a local variable `wgpu::FeatureLevel effectiveFeatureLevel` and use that instead?",
      "revId": "eaee6563db9c8efc7a40dd3fb8a7f5b1f2742450",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "06faa643_41c0092e",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/Device.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 2491,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003446
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-26T18:00:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Once you have a device, all that matters is the features and limits of the device.\n\nThat doesn\u0027t seem true. A compat device has compat validation. a core device doesn\u0027t. The difference is not just features and limits. I\u0027m I mis-understanding?",
      "parentUuid": "2ceef1f7_ca3b60d9",
      "revId": "eaee6563db9c8efc7a40dd3fb8a7f5b1f2742450",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "783ee5d8_5df1c938",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/Device.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 2491,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000014
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-26T18:08:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think that instead of `if (IsCompatibilityMode())` we could do `if (!HasFeature(Feature::CoreFeaturesAndLimits))`.\n\nThough I suppose internally we probably want to keep `IsCompatibilityMode` for convienience/clarity. Maybe I would rename it as `EnforcesCompatibilityMode` or `HasCompatibilityModeValidation`?",
      "parentUuid": "06faa643_41c0092e",
      "revId": "eaee6563db9c8efc7a40dd3fb8a7f5b1f2742450",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
